{"id": "EUVD-2026-95081", "enisaUuid": "e7d8ca82-9b4e-3f2c-acc4-5a7784d9b856", "description": "FFmpeg through 9.0.2 contains an uninitialized memory disclosure vulnerability in av_dynamic_hdr_plus_to_t35() that leaves up to three payload bytes uninitialized when tone_mapping_flag is 0. Attackers can supply crafted Matroska T.35 BlockAdditional or HEVC/AV1 SEI metadata so that remuxing or transcoding writes leaked process memory into output files.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T15:28:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T00:59:55", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/24590", "https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/2c2f6e96e31795ae95a8f8323a493ffbc493111f", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/n9.0.2/libavutil/hdr_dynamic_metadata.c#L374-L385", "https://ffmpeg.org/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ffmpeg-through-9.0.2-uninitialized-memory-disclosure-via-hdr10-metadata-serializer"], "aliases": ["GHSA-77pg-jq65-mg2f", "CVE-2026-107676"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a891b38-a2e7-3ca3-a52b-5007e42ff9fb", "product": {"name": "FFmpeg", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22649.0.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ab4bd3b2-0a04-3706-89ac-0742a333e90c", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}], "isExploited": false}